<title>UK: Prudential off after Britannic payout.</title>
<headline>Prudential off after Britannic payout.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Prudential Corp and Legal &amp; General sank on Tuesday after Britannic Assurance declared a 209 million stg special bonus for life insurance policies.</p>
<p>Dealers and analysts said there appeared to be some switching, which pulled Prudential shares down 6-1/2p to 566-1/2p and Legal &amp; General shares down 8p to 399-1/2. Shares in Britannic, meanwhile, soared 63p to 866-1/2.</p>
</text>
